# Numbers — Memory Drill

## Purpose

Drill digit → Greek number word and reverse. Numbers are 100% arbitrary — no derivation possible, must be recalled from memory. Also presented in /learn/essentials as reference; this is the timed production drill.

Target: 3 seconds digit → word.

Implemented as 28 items in `numbers.tsx` under three categories: 1–10, 11–20, Decades.
Colour theme: terracotta. Returns to `/practice/blocks`.

**Every item is the canonical neuter form** — one form per digit, no variants seeded.
See "Forms deliberately not seeded" below.

## Core sets

### Set A: 1–10 (drill to automaticity before Set B)
| Digit | Greek |
|-------|-------|
| 1 | ένα |
| 2 | δύο |
| 3 | τρία |
| 4 | τέσσερα |
| 5 | πέντε |
| 6 | έξι |
| 7 | εφτά |
| 8 | οχτώ |
| 9 | εννέα |
| 10 | δέκα |

### Set B: 11–20
| Digit | Greek |
|-------|-------|
| 11 | έντεκα |
| 12 | δώδεκα |
| 13 | δεκατρία |
| 14 | δεκατέσσερα |
| 15 | δεκαπέντε |
| 16 | δεκαέξι |
| 17 | δεκαεφτά |
| 18 | δεκαοχτώ |
| 19 | δεκαεννέα |
| 20 | είκοσι |

### Set C: Decades (secondary)
| Digit | Greek |
|-------|-------|
| 30 | τριάντα |
| 40 | σαράντα |
| 50 | πενήντα |
| 60 | εξήντα |
| 70 | εβδομήντα |
| 80 | ογδόντα |
| 90 | ενενήντα |
| 100 | εκατό |

## Drill format

**Forward**: digit display → type Greek word
**Reverse**: Greek word → type digit (fast recognition)

No paradigm table. Sequential or random order. Could add: number reading in context ("I am __ years old" → "Έχω πέντε χρόνια").

## Forms deliberately not seeded

**Gender agreement.** 1, 3, 4 agree (ένας/μία/ένα, τρεις/τρία, τέσσερις/τέσσερα). Only the neuter
is drilled — agreement is a separate grammar concern and belongs in the cases drills, not here.

**Spelling variants.** 7, 8, 9 have two written forms each (εφτά/επτά, οχτώ/οκτώ, εννέα/εννιά).
Only the spoken-preferred form is seeded. If the alternates should be accepted, add them via
`acceptAlso` rather than as extra items — a second item for the same digit would make the reverse
direction ambiguous.

## Notes

- Build order: Set A → Set B → Set C
- Real-world anchors to show after correct answer: "Κάνει πέντε ευρώ" / "Έχω τριάντα χρόνια" — bridges number recall to sentence production
